From 73b434edd4e68abc2757038da6b04fb3cdb93fa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:23:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not load restored tabs in the background on a phone

156 adds kDesktopAndroidBackgroundTabLoading to the desktop Android override
block. Once tabs are restored after a restart, it hands background tabs to
PerformanceManager's BackgroundTabLoadingPolicy, which loads them a few at a
time, up to its own limits on count, age and free memory. Upstream's own
comment says the behaviour is not wanted on mobile Android, but the block is
compiled into every desktop Android build, and Bare is one that runs on phones.

On a phone that means page loads nobody asked for: data, battery and memory.
The memory matters twice over, because memory pressure while Bare is in the
background is what gets uBlock Origin's background page killed. The override is
dropped, so restored tabs load when they are opened, as they did in 153.
kLoadAllTabsAtStartup, which only creates the WebContents, is left as it was.
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_browser_field_trials.cc | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_field_trials.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_field_trials.cc
index 2d638f0cce2..a3341be4e13 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_field_trials.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_field_trials.cc
@@ -279,8 +279,9 @@ void ChromeBrowserFieldTrials::RegisterFeatureOverrides(
   // reloaded. This requires kLoadAllTabsAtStartup above to be enabled as well.
   // This is not enabled elsewhere because the desktop behavior is not desirable
   // on mobile Android.
-  feature_overrides.EnableFeature(
-      chrome::android::kDesktopAndroidBackgroundTabLoading);
+  // Bare: not enabled. This build runs on phones, where loading every
+  // restored tab in the background costs memory, data and battery, and the
+  // memory pressure it adds is what gets extension background pages killed.
 
   // Enable the ability for extensions to override chrome pages.
   // TODO(crbug.com/404069963): Remove flag when the feature is verified to be
